# panel.xrs - the F10 panel reaches BOTH eyes (Ref VR-275, the simple panel).
#
# The panel is drawn into the mono screen's texture, so it must composite in
# the left eye AND the right eye, at the same place. ImGui's dark window counts
# as "black" to the simulator's non-black counter (launch 6: the alley read
# 11.3 percent without the panel and 12.0 with it), so the assertion is a
# CHANGE: the text and widget pixels move the non-black fraction and the mean
# luma by a measurable amount in both eyes, equally, and both fall back when
# the panel closes. A panel drawn in one eye only fails @capsame. The eye
# capture (shot_left.png / shot_right.png under the sim dir) is the picture.
#
# Run it in GAMEPLAY (boot.ps1 first).
reset
@mod overlay off
@frames 30
@shot panel_off
@mod overlay on
@frames 45
@log overlay: OPEN 8s
@shot panel_on
@capchange stats.nonBlackPctL 0.4
@capchange stats.nonBlackPctR 0.4
@capchange stats.meanLumaL 0.2
@capchange stats.meanLumaR 0.2
@capsame stats.nonBlackPctL stats.nonBlackPctR 0.3
@capsame stats.meanLumaL stats.meanLumaR 0.3
@mod overlay off
@frames 45
@shot panel_off2
@capchange stats.nonBlackPctL 0.4
@capchange stats.nonBlackPctR 0.4
